# celestial_bridge's database: password hashes and every trade you have taken.
# It belongs on your machine, not in a repository.
celestial.db
celestial.db-wal
celestial.db-shm
celestial-backup-*.json

# Per-build copies handed to you for download (celestial_alpha_b35.html and
# friends). Each one is a byte-identical duplicate of celestial_alpha_v2_22.html
# at that commit, renamed only so an older copy in the Downloads folder cannot
# be mistaken for the current one. The source file is tracked; the copies are
# 2MB each and the history already holds every build.
celestial_alpha_b*.html
# The single delivered copy. Same name every time, so downloading a new one
# REPLACES the old one in Downloads instead of sitting beside it. Four rounds
# were lost to "nothing changed" when the file on screen was an older build —
# there is only ever one now, and the tab prints its build number.
celestial_alpha.html

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
